<title>USA: Hertz to reopen Sarajevo operations.</title>
<headline>Hertz to reopen Sarajevo operations.</headline>
<dateline>PARK RIDGE, N.J. 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>After a five-year absence during the war in Bosnia and Herzegovina, Hertz Corp said Monday it will reopen operations in downtown Sarajevo on May 1.</p>
<p>The Hertz franchisee, Kompas, which closed all rental locations in the region in 1992, has a new downtown office and will reopen in Sarajevo, Hertz said. Due to heavy damage at Sarajevo airport, which has yet to be rebuilt, the downtown office will service Hertz' airport customers.</p>
<p>The company said it anticipates the reopening of offices in Tuzla and Mostar by late summer.</p>
